Subject: [PATCH] TaskManager: make operator() const for C++20/23 compliance

std::set requires its comparator to be invocable with const arguments.
Since GCC 16 defaults to C++23, libstdc++ enforces this with a
static_assert in <bits/stl_tree.h>. directfb 1.7.7 predates this
requirement.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [project abandoned upstream]

--- a/src/core/TaskManager.h
+++ b/src/core/TaskManager.h
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@ public:
      static void       dumpTasks();
 
 
-     bool operator()( Task *t1, Task *t2 )
+     bool operator()( Task *t1, Task *t2 ) const
      {
           return t1->ts_emit < t2->ts_emit;
      }
